  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Heat the oven to 230°C. Toss 450 g thinly sliced ribeye or sirloin (bulgogi cut) with 2 tbsp soy sauce, 1 tbsp brown sugar, 1 tbsp toasted sesame oil and 2 garlic cloves, grated and marinate while you prep.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        0,
        1,
        2,
        3,
        4
      ],
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Toss 2 carrots, cut into matchsticks, 1 zucchini, cut into half-moons and 200 g shiitake mushrooms, sliced separately with 3 tbsp neutral oil and 1/2 tsp salt, and spread them in their own sections on a large sheet pan. Roast 12 minutes.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        5,
        6,
        7,
        8,
        9
      ],
      "timers": [
        {
          "text": "12 minutes",
          "seconds": 720
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Push the vegetables together and spread the beef on the free part of the pan in a thin layer. Roast 6 minutes more, until the beef is cooked and the vegetables are browned at the edges.",
      "ingredientRefs": [],
      "timers": [
        {
          "text": "6 minutes",
          "seconds": 360
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, wilt 200 g baby spinach in a hot pan for 1 minute and toss with 1 tsp toasted sesame oil (for the spinach) and a pinch of salt. Whisk 3 tbsp gochujang, 1 tbsp toasted sesame oil (for the sauce), 1 tbsp rice vinegar, 1 tbsp honey and 1 tbsp water.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        10,
        11,
        12,
        13,
        14,
        15,
        16
      ],
      "timers": [
        {
          "text": "1 minute",
          "seconds": 60
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fry 4 eggs sunny side up for 3 minutes, until the whites are crisp at the edges.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        18
      ],
      "timers": [
        {
          "text": "3 minutes",
          "seconds": 180
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Divide 900 g hot cooked short-grain rice among bowls and arrange the beef, vegetables, spinach and 200 g kimchi on top in sections. Top with an egg, sauce and 1 tbsp toasted sesame seeds. Mix everything together before eating.",
      "ingredientRefs": [
        17,
        19,
        20
      ],
      "timers": []
    }
  ],
  "notes": "For dolsot-style crispy rice, press the rice into a hot oiled cast-iron pan and cook undisturbed for 8 minutes before topping. Bean sprouts (blanched 2 minutes, dressed with sesame oil and salt) are a classic addition.",
